%N A399448 Triangle read by rows: T(n,k) is the number of simple connected graphs on n nodes having k distinct vertex transmissions.
%C A399448 The vertex transmission of a vertex is the sum of the distances to all other vertices.
%C A399448 The number of distinct vertex transmissions can also be called the transmission dimension of the graph.
